1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:02,470
You're watching them open Napoleon's coffin,

2
00:00:02,470 --> 00:00:04,720
19 years after he died.

3
00:00:05,170 --> 00:00:05,960
What did they find?

4
00:00:06,563 --> 00:00:09,523
May 1821. Napoleon Bonaparte,

5
00:00:09,523 --> 00:00:11,013
once the master of Europe,

6
00:00:11,263 --> 00:00:13,273
dies in exile on Saint Helena,

7
00:00:13,543 --> 00:00:15,273
a rock in the South Atlantic.

8
00:00:15,789 --> 00:00:17,249
He is buried in a quiet valley,

9
00:00:17,249 --> 00:00:18,949
under heavy stone slabs,

10
00:00:18,949 --> 00:00:21,659
in four coffins, one inside another.

11
00:00:22,146 --> 00:00:24,446
Nineteen years later, France wants its emperor

12
00:00:24,446 --> 00:00:27,296
back. At midnight in October 1840,

13
00:00:27,966 --> 00:00:30,486
by torchlight, British soldiers begin to

14
00:00:30,486 --> 00:00:30,876
dig.

15
00:00:31,277 --> 00:00:33,037
It takes them hours to break through the

16
00:00:33,037 --> 00:00:35,687
stone. Coffin after coffin is opened.

17
00:00:36,217 --> 00:00:37,347
When the last lid lifts,

18
00:00:37,497 --> 00:00:39,567
the witnesses see only a white shape.

19
00:00:39,897 --> 00:00:40,927
They fear the worst.

20
00:00:41,518 --> 00:00:43,638
Then the ship's surgeon slowly rolls back

21
00:00:43,638 --> 00:00:46,198
a sheet of white satin that had fallen from

22
00:00:46,198 --> 00:00:46,708
the lid.

23
00:00:47,081 --> 00:00:49,351
Napoleon's face is instantly recognizable.

24
00:00:50,241 --> 00:00:52,711
Eyes closed. Eyelashes still there.

25
00:00:53,101 --> 00:00:55,071
His green uniform, almost perfect.

26
00:00:55,501 --> 00:00:57,401
The red ribbon of the Legion of Honor,

27
00:00:57,401 --> 00:00:58,771
still across his chest.

28
00:00:59,448 --> 00:01:01,158
Nineteen years after his death,

29
00:01:01,488 --> 00:01:03,238
the Emperor looked like he was asleep.

30
00:01:03,839 --> 00:01:05,779
That December, Paris carried him through

31
00:01:05,779 --> 00:01:07,799
its freezing streets to Les Invalides,

32
00:01:07,799 --> 00:01:09,349
where he lies today.

33
00:01:09,851 --> 00:01:10,931
How did his body survive?

34
00:01:10,931 --> 00:01:13,791
Arsenic, some say. Others point to four

35
00:01:13,791 --> 00:01:15,901
sealed coffins. What do you think?

36
00:01:16,071 --> 00:01:17,421
Follow Buried Chronicles.

